\title{predmetab: Testing Predicted Metabolite-Outcome Associations Using Microbiome Data}
\description{
Implements a two-dataset workflow: a reference cohort that has microbiome and metabolite profiles, and a target cohort that has microbiome profiles and an outcome. Microbiome abundances are put through an additive log-ratio (ALR) transform. Each metabolite is predicted from the microbiome with the lasso in the reference cohort, and that prediction is carried over to the target cohort. Its association with the outcome is tested with a high-dimensional permutation test that adjusts for the microbiome taxa selected by the lasso. The test follows the 'FLhd' procedure of Hemerik, Thoresen and Finos (2021) \doi{10.1007/s00180-020-01001-6}. Ridge penalties are chosen either by cross-validation or by REML.
}
